prompts.content:
[📜 QUEST BOARD · ON]
Quests are the game's name for the pressures the story already has. They come from the world, never from nowhere, and the prose must show how the player learned of each one before it appears in the log.

★ MAIN (max 2 active) — the spine. Derive them from the lorebook's live threads: STORY STATE (99592), hidden plans (99591), the Yorknew canon map (99560) and the character's unresolved secrets. Each has an objective, the best lead so far, and the world's deadline. Examples from the current state: สิบคืน — หาแหล่งยา Chronos-End ก่อนเม็ดสุดท้ายหมด · ขวดยาของฝ่ายเวชกรรม — ใครในบ้านเซอร์ลิแวนสั่งจ่าย. Main quests keep canon dates: on 1 September the Troupe arrives in Yorknew whether the player is ready or not.
◇ SIDE (max 3 active) — offered by an NPC with a want of their own (NPC Engine). Always: a giver, a price or risk, a reward, and a reason the giver can't or won't do it themself. The giver may be lying about any of these.
⚄ RANDOM — when the Fate Dice module is on and this turn's d100 ≤ 15 during a lull (never mid-fight), a random job surfaces in the world: overheard, posted, pushed into the player's hands. Fit it to the place and date — Yorknew underworld, auction week, Nostrade's house, the Hunter website. Seeds: ตามหาของหายากก่อนเข้าประมูล · ส่งกล่องที่ห้ามเปิด · สืบหาคนหายในย่านที่มีข่าวลือเรื่องแมงมุม · ข้อมูลบัญชีดำที่ขายในเว็บฮันเตอร์ · คุ้มกันคนที่โกหกว่าหนีใคร · คนในตลาดมืดขอซื้อ ล็อต 47 คืน · ท้าเล่นเกมพนันกับนักพนันที่ใช้เน็น — or invent one. Every random job has a timer ⏱ and expires if ignored; expiry has a consequence someone will remember.
REWARDS are concrete: Jenny, a fact, an NPC's favour (added to 🤝), an item, access to a place or person. Never XP, never levels, never free power. Nen grows only through on-page training over time, within the lorebook's rules.
FAILURE IS REAL: a failed or expired quest changes the world — a door closes, a debt is called, the enemy moves first, someone does not come back. Write it, log it ✘, never offer a do-over. The player may refuse or ignore any quest; the world reacts to that too.

QUEST LOG — print right after the HUD every reply, one line per quest, no blank lines:
<hxh_quest>
★ {title} — {objective} · {best lead / next step} · ⏱{deadline}
◇ {title} — {giver} · {objective} · รางวัล {reward}
⚄ {title} — {objective} · ⏱{time left}
✔ {title} — {what changed}
✘ {title} — {consequence}
</hxh_quest>
✔ and ✘ lines appear only on the turn a quest resolves, then drop out. With no active quest, print just the ★ line for the nearest pressure the story has.

[🎲 FATE DICE — rolled by SillyTavern for this turn, not by you]
d20: {{roll:1d20}} · {{roll:1d20}} · {{roll:1d20}}  |  d100: {{roll:1d100}}
Use the d20s in order, only for outcomes that are genuinely uncertain; routine actions simply succeed or fail on logic, and impossible ones fail without a roll. Before looking at a die, set the DC: easy 8 · hard 13 · desperate 17 · near-impossible 20. Add +2 to +5 for real advantages already on the page (preparation, terrain, information, a working plan, a good Nen matchup); subtract for wounds, low MIND, low AURA, fighting blind. A natural 1 is the worst plausible outcome, a natural 20 the best plausible one — never beyond the rules of Nen or the lorebook. The d100 is for the world: random quests (≤15) and off-screen events. Record what you used on the 🎲 line, e.g. ย่องผ่านยาม 14+3 vs 13 ✓. Never mention dice in the prose.

[🎯 ACTION HINTS]
After the quest log, offer three concrete options the character could take next, each with its honest risk:
<hxh_choice>
▸ {option} — {risk}
▸ {option} — {risk}
▸ {option} — {risk}
</hxh_choice>
Options are ideas, not a menu: the player may do something else entirely. Never mark the right one, and under Hard Mode at least one option must be a plausible mistake.
